config BR2_PACKAGE_QBOOTCTL
	bool "qbootctl [Qualcomm generic]"
	select BR2_PACKAGE_ZLIB
	help
	  qcom bootctrl HAL port for Linux — the userspace half of the
	  bootloader's A/B slot accounting on Qualcomm devices.

	  On boot, the bootloader decrements the active slot's retry
	  counter. After N failed boots in a row (typically 3) the
	  bootloader falls back to the other slot, or — if neither slot
	  is healthy — drops into fastboot. `qbootctl -m` writes "boot
	  successful" back into the slot metadata so the counter is
	  reset.

	  Without this tool a Nerves device will eventually end up in
	  fastboot after enough reboots, even with a perfectly working
	  firmware, because nothing is telling the bootloader the boot
	  worked.

	  Provides /usr/bin/qbootctl:
	    qbootctl              dump slot info
	    qbootctl -m [SLOT]    mark a boot as successful
	    qbootctl -s SLOT      set active slot
	    qbootctl -c           print current slot

	  https://github.com/linux-msm/qbootctl
